From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rbb-dev <37469229+rbb-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:57:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: a prompt pass in flight shows on /health and /metrics,
 its tokens and speed so far

A long prompt's pass runs inside its admission and reported nothing until it ended: /health's
prefill_tokens_per_second read 0 for the whole pass (70 s at 200K tokens) and showed the pass's speed only for
the 2 s after it, so a dashboard never saw a prefill running. Now the backend stores the rows it has passed after
each chunk (Stream.progress: one atomic store a 2,048-row chunk, no lock, no GPU wait; dsv41 is the first backend
to do it) and the lane host reports the pass while it runs:
- /health live: prefill_tokens_per_second is the running pass's speed so far (the last pass's for 2 s after, as
  before); prompt_pass = {computed, total, resumed, seconds} (null between passes); prompt_tokens_computed_total.
- /metrics: tensorfold:prompt_tokens_computed_total (a counter, the running pass's tokens included: its rate is the
  prefill speed; a pass that fails or is cancelled keeps what it computed, so it never goes back), and the gauges
  prompt_pass_tokens_computed, _total and _resumed (0 between passes).
An engine that reports no passes (other families) leaves /health as it was and adds no /metrics family.

Tests: stream.zig (only computed rows count, never resumed ones); lane_host_test (a pass's progress mid-pass
through the fake backend, which now reports its chunks; the counter after the pass, and after a pass cancelled at
its 4th chunk); live.zig and metrics.zig (the fields and families, and none for an engine without passes). Each
new test was seen to fail with its code broken. Server suite 67 + 31 pass; zig build test as before (dsv41's
debug build stops on prompt.zig's genSetReg, direct_io's O_DIRECT test fails on WSL); engine-check: aarch64
tensorfold-native builds, dsv41 suite (LLVM) 120 pass, 1 fails, the same 1 as without this commit.
